course: dictionary
lesson: 6179
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. «Minus» is a good example. It can mean take away, below zero, or a bad point, and you can tell which one is meant by looking at the words around it. Look for the numbers, the grade or the list of points.
explain: «Mercury's daytime surface reaches about 430 degrees Celsius, but at night it falls to about minus 180.» Here minus comes before a number and tells you the temperature is below zero. Minus 180 is much colder than zero, not 180 taken away from something.
explain: «Draw a table; "score = 7, minus 2, times 3, plus 1" goes 7, 5, 15, 16.» Here minus means take away, so 7 minus 2 is 5. Always ask: does the word fit as take away, below zero, or a bad point? Then try that meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Sometimes minus is a noun, as in «pluses and minuses». Then a minus is a disadvantage, a bad point. Minus can also come after a grade, as in «B minus», which means a bit lower than a B. The same small word, three different jobs.
fact: Minus means take away, as in 7 minus 3 is 4.
fact: The sign for minus is −, and it is used for subtraction.
fact: Minus before a number means below zero, as in minus 5 degrees, which is colder than zero.
fact: A minus is a bad point or disadvantage, as in «pluses and minuses».
fact: After a grade, minus means a bit lower: «B minus» is a little lower than a B.
exercise: «Mercury's night temperature falls to about minus 180.» What does minus mean here? | A bit lower than a grade | *Below zero | Take away | A bad point
exercise: Ella says, «The pluses and minuses of the plan were clear.» What is a minus in this sentence? | *A bad point or disadvantage | A very cold day | A way to add numbers | A number on a sign
exercise: «Score = 7, minus 2, times 3, plus 1» goes 7, 5, 15, 16. What does minus 2 do to 7? | *Takes away 2, giving 5 | Adds 2, giving 9 | Multiplies 7 by 2 | Makes the score negative
test: The temperature was minus 39 degrees on Monday and minus 40 degrees on Tuesday. Which day was colder? | Monday | Neither, because minus means nothing | *Tuesday | They were the same
test: In «B minus», what does minus show about the grade? | It is a bit higher than a B | It means take away the B | It means the B was wrong | *It is a bit lower than a B
exam: Which sentence uses minus to mean below zero? | There were pluses and minuses to the trip. | Ten minus four makes six. | She got a B minus for her story. | *It fell to minus 5 degrees overnight.
